		<p>The Paediatrics and Neonatology Department at GEIMS specialises in the healthcare of infants, children, and adolescents, covering a spectrum of medical needs from routine check-ups to critical care interventions.</p><p>This department equips students with comprehensive knowledge in child development, pediatric diseases, and neonatal care. Students engage in hands-on learning, participating in clinical rotations, pediatric wards, and neonatal units, gaining exposure to diverse cases under the guidance of experienced paediatricians.</p><p>Emphasis is placed on nurturing compassionate care, effective communication with young patients and their families, and understanding the unique medical, emotional, and social needs of pediatric and neonatal populations.</p><p> </p><p><strong>Key Highlights</strong></p><p>The Department of Paediatrics and Neonatology specialises in child health. Clinical training, developmental expertise, and compassionate care skills prepare students for comprehensive pediatric practice and neonatal care.</p><ul><li><strong>Comprehensive Clinical Exposure: </strong>Engaging rotations in pediatric wards and neonatal units, providing firsthand experience with various pediatric specialities<strong>.</strong></li></ul><ul><li><strong>Interactive Learning:</strong> Interactive sessions covering developmental milestones, pediatric illnesses, and specialised neonatal care, foster a deep understanding of child health.</li><li><strong>Emphasis on Compassionate Care: </strong>Focus on empathy in patient interactions, honing communication skills tailored to connect with children and their families.</li><li><strong>Diverse Practical Experiences: </strong>Opportunities for research and hands-on experiences across different pediatric settings, preparing us for versatile pediatric care.</li></ul>		
			<h5>Department Info</h5>		
		<p>Department of Paediatrics and Neonatology</p><p>Graphic Era Institute of Medical Sciences<br />16th Milestone, Chakrata Rd, Dehradun, Uttarakhand 248008</p>		
