		<p>The Community Medicine Department immerses students in public health, preventive medicine, and community healthcare strategies. It equips future healthcare professionals with tools to address population health challenges through research, education, and community involvement. This student-centric environment fosters practical skills and critical thinking essential for shaping the future of healthcare. Opportunities abound in diverse sectors, from public health organisations to policymaking bodies, offering pathways for impactful careers in epidemiology, health education, community outreach, and healthcare administration. Students emerge adept at designing interventions, driving public health policies, and spearheading initiatives that positively impact communities in the evolving healthcare landscape.</p><p> </p><p><strong>Key Highlights</strong></p><p>The Community Medicine Department emphasises public health education, community engagement, and research initiatives. Through these pillars, students gain expertise in population health, paving the way for diverse and impactful careers in healthcare and public health sectors.</p><ul><li><strong>Public Health Education: </strong>Extensive learning in public health strategies and preventive medicine.</li><li><strong>Community Engagement:</strong> Involvement in healthcare interventions and community-based programs.</li><li><strong>Research Emphasis: </strong>Focus on studying population health and implementing effective interventions.</li><li><strong>Career Diversity: </strong>Opportunities in epidemiology, health education, policy-making, and community healthcare.</li></ul>		
			<h5>Department Info</h5>		
		<p>Department of Community Medicine</p><p>Graphic Era Institute of Medical Sciences<br />16th Milestone, Chakrata Rd, Dehradun, Uttarakhand 248008</p>		
